A while back, there was some mention of custom-designing special
levels for NH and distributing them as patches over this newsgroup.
Did that generate any interest?  I, for one, wouldn't mind seeing it,
or even entire "modules" for NH:  whole "quests" (like the Gnomish
Mines/the Quest, etc.) where you could meet unique creatures (or
armies of particular creatures), get particular artifacts/powerful
mundane items, and even have to solve special puzzles (like navigate a
maze of teleport traps, teleport control rendered ineffectual).

These modules could either branch off from the Dungeon of Doom
(randomly or all the time;  don't worry if they disrupt game balance,
because if a module is too easy or too hard for you, just delete the
patch.  We could rate modules for difficulty here so that people won't
pick modules that make the game too hard or easy for their taste) or
be playable as completely separate games that maintain their own
scorelist but use the basic NH rules (and share much of the same code,
so it wouldn't be like writing a whole new game).  NH is a pretty hard
game, and I wouldn't want it to get too much easier (keep the
challenge going), but having "baby nethack" adventures that we mortals
could win before we've reached the skill level required to become True
Demigods would be nice.

I'd offer to try my hand myself if I were a better programmer;  maybe
I'll come up with a design and see if anyone here is willing to code
it for a share of the glory (probably most of it, as judging from the
recent posts about opaque NH code, it will probably be most of the
work).

Anyway, what do people think of these ideas?

